From f9f11d925490f58c5cb7e1794d1f8fe474c8e902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:32:23 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH v2 8/8] ksmbd: experiment with RX-owned WRITE response
 sending

WRITE workers can contend with the receiver on the same TCP socket.
Let the receiver drain completed WRITE responses, controlled by the
default-off write_tx_rx_owner parameter.

Use nonblocking sends in RX and resume partial batches on a separate TX
workqueue, preventing other responses from entering an unfinished frame.
The continuation hands sending back to RX without dropping the owner
reference. RX rechecks ownership under write_tx_lock before draining or
releasing it. Share batch handling with worker TX and retain its budget.

Built with W=1. Extracted-function tests passed under ASan/UBSan. Kernel
transport checks using invalid-session requests passed FIN, paused-reader,
mixed-response, reset and shutdown cases, including short-send recovery.
Throughput validation of this version remains pending.

Signed-off-by: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
